<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Partium</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Partium was the group of eastern counties of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-hungary">Kingdom of Hungary</a>, around Nagyvárad (Oradea) and Szatmár, that were ruled by the princes of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/transylvania">Transylvania</a> from the 16th century, as confirmed by the Treaty of Speyer in 1570. The name means 'parts' of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a>. The area is now divided between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romania">Romania</a>, Hungary and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ukraine">Ukraine</a>.</p></div>
